Conceptual verification statement (framework framing only):
Ownership may be expressed under the Boundary-Horizon Framework as a finite
residual boundary between the full authorship domain and the operational domain
of permitted use:

    Ω_out - Ω_in = H

where Ω_out denotes the full authorship domain, Ω_in denotes the bounded
domain of permitted use under this license, and H denotes the finite residual
rights retained by the authors. This formulation is conceptual and explanatory
only; it does not alter the legal terms of this license.

